# Leonardo's permission has a limit and a place. Faithless Looting discards Grizzly Bears (2/2, one past the limit on both
# counts) on turn 1; Bot2's graveyard gets a Cathar Commando from its hand-size discard. On turn 3 Bot1, with {1}{G} and the
# rest, cannot cast the Bears from the graveyard (the refusal) nor Bot2's Commando (the refusal), and a Savannah Lions cast from
# hand for {W} enters with no finality counter: only a spell cast by Leonardo's permission gets one.

